      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "Opening hand: Allies at Last (2G), Flopsie Bumi's Buddy (4GG), Iguana Parrot (2U), Island, Island, Island, Knowledge Seeker (1U).\n\
\n\
That's 3 Islands, no green sources, and two green cards. Hand has blue creatures playable: Knowledge Seeker turn 1, Iguana Parrot turn 2... wait, three Islands means turn 2 Iguana Parrot needs UU — 2U = {2}{U}, needs one blue + two generic. Turn 2 with two Islands I can play Knowledge Seeker turn 1 ({1}{U} needs 1U = two mana — turn 1 only one Island, can't play it). Turn 1: Island, no play. Turn 2: Island, Knowledge Seeker. Turn 3: Island, Iguana Parrot.\n\
\n\
But two green cards are dead without Forests. Deck is 33 cards, presumably green-blue. Keeping a 7-card hand with 3 lands and only blue spells castable early... The green cards need green mana. There are likely Forests in the deck. This hand is mediocre but has plays. Risk: keeping means relying on drawing Forests for the two green cards.\n\
\n\
Mulligan to 6 could get a better mix. But this hand has 3 lands and 4 spells, curve is okay for blue. Allies at Last needs 2G and allies on board (affinity). Flopsie needs 4GG — hard even with Forests.\n\
\n\
I think this is a keepable but weak hand. Standard advice: 3 lands + playable spells = keep. The green cards might be dead for a while, but Knowledge Seeker and Iguana Parrot give early board presence. In a 40-card deck (33 library + 7 hand), this looks like Avatar-themed limited. Let me keep.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider: with 3 Islands and needing GG for Flopsie and G for Allies, I need to draw Forests. If the deck is UG with maybe 8-9 Forests, decent chance to draw one in a few turns. Keeping gives Knowledge Seeker turn 2, Iguana turn 3. That's fine. I'll keep.",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "name": "choose_action",
          "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Opening hand has 3 Islands, two castable blue creatures (Knowledge Seeker, Iguana Parrot), and two green cards I can't cast yet. Keepable curve with lands and early plays.\",\"choice\":\"no\",\"rationale\":\"Keeping: 3 lands with a turn-2 Knowledge Seeker and turn-3 Iguana Parrot gives me early board presence. The green cards are dead until I find a Forest, but the blue core is functional.\"}",
        }
