      "reasoning": "I'll play my Island first (land drop), then cast Forecasting Fortune Teller — it's a creature so Mai won't punish it, and its 1/3 body survives blocking Mai's 2 first-strike damage. The Clue token also sets up future card draw to fuel Knowledge Seeker.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the board state.\n\
\n\
My board: 2 Islands (untapped), Knowledge Seeker 2/1.\n\
Opponent: Abandoned Air Temple, Mai Scornful Striker 2/2 (tapped), Pretending Poxbearers 2/1 (sick), 2 Swamps (tapped). Life 20. Hand 4.\n\
\n\
I have 2 mana. I can cast Forecasting Fortune Teller (1/3, creates Clue on ETB). But opponent has Mai which punishes noncreature spells — Forecasting Fortune Teller is a creature, so no penalty. Good.\n\
\n\
Should I play the land first? I have 2 Islands in hand. Playing a land: I have an Island in hand. Playing a land gives me 3 mana but then I can't use it this turn for anything except... Iguana Parrot is {2}{U} = 3 mana. Katara is {2}{U} = 3 mana. So if I play a land, I can't cast a 2-drop this turn. If I cast Fortune Teller now, I can play the land too (one land drop). Actually I can play land AND cast Fortune Teller: 2 mana from existing islands.\n\
\n\
Best: play Island (land drop), then cast Forecasting Fortune Teller {1}{U} using two of my three lands. That leaves one Island untapped... no wait, 3 islands total, cast Fortune Teller costs 2, leaves 1 untapped.\n\
\n\
Actually order doesn't matter much. Play Island first (free), then cast Fortune Teller. That gives me a 1/3 blocker that creates a Clue. The Clue can be sacrificed later for card draw (but cracking Clue is a noncreature... no, sacrificing a Clue is an activated ability, not a spell, so Mai doesn't trigger). Good.\n\
\n\
Forecasting Fortune Teller 1/3 is a decent blocker against Mai's 2/2 first strike — blocks and survives (1/3 takes 2 first strike damage, survives with 1 toughness left). Great.\n\
\n\
Let me play Island first.",
