      "reasoning": "Opponent's Corrupt Court Official is making me discard. Let me think about what I can afford to lose.\n\
\n\
My plan this turn: cast Allies at Last (costs {1}{G} with my Ally discount) to kill Mai — prowess makes Iguana Parrot 3/3, so it deals 3 + Fortune Teller's 1 = 4 damage, more than enough. I keep all my spells for that. Flopsie needs double green plus 6 mana (I only have one Forest), so I need to draw more lands regardless — and I have two Clue tokens to dig for them. The Island is the lowest-impact card.",
      "thinking": "Opponent cast Corrupt Court Official, and its ETB trigger makes me discard a card. I must choose what to discard from: Allies at Last, Flopsie, Bumi's Buddy, Island, Katara, Bending Prodigy.\n\
\n\
My plan was to cast Allies at Last next turn to kill Mai. I have 4 lands (3 Islands tapped + 1 Forest untapped? wait, board says Forest untapped, 3 Islands tapped). Actually this turn (turn 5) I'll untap. I have 4 lands total, so next turn 5 mana? No wait — it's my turn 5 precombat main, but lands are tapped? Actually the board shows my lands tapped from last turn... hmm, actually the snapshot shows turn 5 precombat main with lands tapped. Odd — maybe the discard decision is happening before untap? Actually Corrupt Court Official ETB trigger targets me — opponent cast it on their turn 4? Wait, it's Turn 5 precombat main for me, PilotA. The stack has Corrupt Court Official's ETB trigger targeting me.\n\
\n\
Wait, the turn log: opponent's turn 4 they cast Corrupt Court Official presumably, and the trigger... Actually it says Turn 5 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - PilotA with my lands tapped. That seems like maybe the display. Regardless, I must discard.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- Discard Island: I have 4 lands in play already, 5th land not critical? But I want to hit 6 mana for Flopsie eventually, and Katara costs 2U. Discarding Island keeps all spells.\n\
- Discard Allies at Last: my plan to kill Mai.\n\
- Discard Katara: a solid 2/3 but I'm fine.\n\
- Discard Flopsie: 6-mana top end, far away with only 4 lands.\n\
\n\
Opponent has 14 hp. My board: Fortune Teller 1/3, Iguana Parrot 2/2 flying vigilance prowess.\n\
\n\
Iguana Parrot is an evasive clock. Allies at Last lets Fortune Teller (1) + Iguana (2) = 3 damage to kill Mai (2 toughness). That clears the way for Iguana attacks (Mai has first strike, can't block flyers anyway — Mai doesn't have flying, so Mai can't block Iguana Parrot). Actually Mai can't block the flying Iguana at all! So Allies at Last to kill Mai is less critical for my air attack. But Mai's attacks punish me.\n\
\n\
What do I value least? I have 4 lands in play, drawing Island in hand. Flopsie costs {4}{G}{G} — I only have one Forest, so double green is hard. I need more Forests. Katara {2}{U} is castable.\n\
\n\
Honestly, the Island is the most disposable? But hitting land drops for Flopsie/Katara + Allies at Last... I have 4 lands; if I discard Island, I'm stuck at 4 mana for a while. With 4 mana: Allies at Last costs {2}{G} - 1 (affinity, 1 Ally) = {1}{G}. Easily castable. Katara costs {2}{U} = 3 mana. Flopsie needs 6 mana with GG — I have only 1 Forest. Flopsie is basically uncastable for a long time (need 2 Forests + 6 lands). \n\
\n\
Discard Flopsie? It's my biggest late-game threat but I need GG and 6 mana. With one Forest in play and Island in hand, I'd need to draw another Forest plus more lands. That's far off. Meanwhile opponent's enchantment engine is building up. Hmm, but Flopsie gives +1/+1 counters to all and can't be blocked by more than one — it's a real finisher.\n\
\n\
Actually, let's think: what does the opponent's board look like? Mai 2/2 first strike, Corrupt Court Official 1/1, two Ally tokens 1/1. They have Obsessive Pursuit (lose 1 life each upkeep, make Clues) and Tolls of War (sacrificing permanents makes Ally tokens). They're at 14 and losing 1/turn from Obsessive Pursuit, plus Mai taxes their noncreature spells.\n\
\n\
My plan: Iguana Parrot attacks in the air for 2/turn. They're at 14, so 7 turns. They lose 1/turn to Obsessive Pursuit. That's a decent clock.\n\
\n\
Discard choice: I'd discard the Island or Flopsie. Keeping Katara gives me a 2/3 body that grows and a card-draw engine late. Keeping Allies at Last kills Mai (or clears blockers). \n\
\n\
Land count: I have 4 lands, 4 cards in hand after discard. If I discard Island, next draw steps need to find lands for Flopsie. But honestly Flopsie needs GG; with one Forest I need another Forest anyway. The Island doesn't help cast Flopsie's GG. But it helps get to 6 mana total.\n\
\n\
I think discarding Island is safest — keeps all my action. With 4 lands I can cast everything except Flopsie, and Flopsie needs a second Forest regardless. Wait — but if I keep Island and play it, I have 5 mana; drawing one Forest lets me... still not 6. Need 2 more land drops for Flopsie either way. So the Island in hand only matters if I hit my land drops otherwise. With 29 cards left, I'll draw lands. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Alternatively discard Flopsie — the card I'll cast last. By the time I have 6 mana with GG, the game may be decided. But Flopsie is a huge bomb: +1/+1 counter to each creature, and 4-power creatures can't be blocked by more than one. With Iguana becoming 3/3 (prowess) and getting a counter to 4/4... it ends games.\n\
\n\
Let me think about Mai's tax: I cast few noncreature spells. Allies at Last is noncreature — but opponent controls Mai, so *I* lose 2 life when I cast Allies at Last. Wait, Mai: \"Whenever a player casts a noncreature spell, they lose 2 life.\" So I lose 2 casting Allies at Last. Still worth it to kill Mai (2/2 first strike that threatens me and taxes me).\n\
\n\
Plan: discard Island. Then this turn: untap, draw, play... wait, it's my precombat main with lands tapped? The display shows tapped lands but it's turn 5 precombat — maybe the trigger resolved during opponent's turn and the display is stale, or actually maybe the game just shows. Untapped lands: 1 (the Forest). Hmm, \"Untapped lands: 1\". So this is happening on MY turn 5 precombat main with lands still tapped?? That can't be. More likely opponent cast Corrupt Court Official at my end step or... Actually wait, maybe opponent's turn isn't over — no, it says Turn 5 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - PilotA. \n\
\n\
Oh I see — maybe opponent flash-cast or the Official was cast during my turn? No. Probably the board display shows lands tapped because I haven't... no, untap happens automatically. Let me not overthink; the \"untapped lands: 1\" likely reflects something odd, but after I discard I'll see the real state. Actually, maybe it's still showing opponent's end-of-turn-4 state and the Corrupt Official was cast on opponent's turn 4, with the trigger on the stack targeting me, and the game waited for my discard choice before passing to my turn? But it says Turn 5 PilotA precombat main. Whatever — decide the discard.\n\
\n\
Decision: Discard the Island. Reasoning: I have 4 lands in play which covers Allies at Last (1G with discount) and Katara (2U). Flopsie needs a second Forest plus 6 mana, so the Island alone doesn't unlock it; I need to draw more lands regardless, and my Clue tokens can help dig. Keep all spells.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but counterpoint: if I never draw another land, I'm stuck at 4 and can't cast Flopsie even with a Forest. Discarding Flopsie removes that concern entirely and keeps my land density for consistent drops + Clue cracking. Which is better against their deck? They're building an Ally token army with Tolls of War + Clues. Flopsie's \"can't be blocked by more than one\" doesn't help vs tokens that much, but the 4/4 body + counters does.\n\
\n\
Actually, my Iguana Parrot already flies over their ground tokens. The Ally tokens can't block flyers. So my air clock is fine. What I fear: their ground army + Mai attacking me. Fortune Teller walls Mai (first strike 2 damage into 1/3 — Mai survives? Mai deals 2 first-strike to 1/3 Fortune Teller, Fortune Teller survives with 1 toughness left and deals 1 back). Good wall.\n\
\n\
Allies at Last kill on Mai: Fortune Teller 1 + Iguana 2 = 3 damage, and prowess triggers on Iguana when I cast it (noncreature spell) making Iguana 3/3, so actually damage dealt equals power at resolution — prowess triggers on cast, so by resolution Iguana is 3/3, dealing 3 + 1 = 4. Kills Mai easily. Also I lose 2 life to Mai's trigger. Worth it.\n\
\n\
Given the plan to cast Allies at Last this turn (costs {1}{G}, I have Forest + Islands), I keep it. Katara is a fine follow-up. Flopsie is the luxury.\n\
\n\
Final: discard Island. Keep spells; I have 4 mana which casts everything but Flopsie, and I have 2 Clues to crack for more cards/lands.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — one more consideration. If I discard Island, hand = Allies at Last, Flopsie, Katara. This turn: 4 mana. Cast Allies at Last ({1}{G}) killing Mai, leaving {2}{U}... wait, 3 Islands + 1 Forest = 4 mana. Allies at Last with 1 Ally costs {1}{G} = 2 mana. Then Katara {2}{U} = 3 mana. Total 5 — can't do both. Choose Allies at Last to kill Mai this turn, then attack with Iguana (vigilance, flies — can't be blocked by Mai anyway). Then next turn Katara.\n\
\n\
Alternatively cast Katara this turn, Allies next turn. But killing Mai now stops its attacks and their... Mai taxes them too, they might like it gone. But it's their card; it's been taxing me 2 per noncreature spell. I don't cast many noncreatures, but Mai attacking for 2 first strike each turn is the threat. Kill it now.\n\
\n\
Also note I lose 2 life casting Allies at Last (18 → 16). Fine.\n\
\n\
So: choose_action choice=\"p23\" (discard Island).\n\
\n\
Wait, actually should I discard Flopsie instead? Let me commit: discard Island. Hmm, but then I have only 4 lands and my hand is all spells costing 2-6. If I don't draw lands, Flopsie is dead anyway. The Island keeps mana development going. Ugh.\n\
\n\
Simple heuristic: discard the card with the least impact. Iguana flies over everything; Allies at Last kills Mai; Katara is a growing threat + card draw; Flopsie is a finisher that needs GG (I have 1 Forest, need to draw another); Island is a land when I have 4 in play and 2 Clues to draw more.\n\
\n\
With 2 Clue tokens, hitting land drops is easy (crack Clues). So Island is the least impactful? But cracking a Clue costs 2 mana + it's noncreature... no, activating Clue ability isn't casting a spell, so no Mai tax. Good.\n\
\n\
I'll discard the Island. If I draw a Forest later, 4 mana + Forest = 5... still short of 6 for Flopsie. I need 2 more lands regardless of this Island. So Island's marginal value is low. Confirmed: discard Island (p23).\n\
\n\
