      "reasoning": "Mai has first strike as a 3/3 now — blocking with either creature loses it for free (Fortune Teller's 3 toughness dies to 3 first-strike damage without dealing any back). I'd rather take the 3 damage, keep my board, and kill Mai with Allies at Last on my turn (Fortune Teller 1 + Iguana 2 + prowess bonus = lethal).",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the situation. It's turn 5, opponent's turn. They attacked with Mai, Scornful Striker (now a 3/3 with a +1/+1 counter from Obsessive Pursuit — they sacrificed a Clue this turn, X=1, so Mai gets +1/+1).\n\
\n\
Wait, actually Mai was 2/2 base... Let me check. Mai is listed as \"3/3 (tapped, 1 +1/+1 counter, included in 3/3)\". So Mai is a 2/2 with one +1/+1 counter = 3/3. First strike. Obsessive Pursuit trigger: X = permanents sacrificed this turn = 1 (they cracked a Clue presumably), so Mai got a counter.\n\
\n\
I'm at 18 hp. Opponent is at 14 hp.\n\
\n\
My board: Forecasting Fortune Teller 1/3, Iguana Parrot 2/2 (sick — can't block... wait, summoning sick creatures CAN block, they just can't attack or use tap abilities. Actually, summoning sickness prevents attacking and activating abilities with tap/untap symbols. Blocking is fine. But the interface lists Iguana Parrot as a choice, so it can block).\n\
\n\
Mai has first strike and is 3/3. If I block with Fortune Teller (1/3), first strike damage: Mai deals 3 to Fortune Teller, killing it. Fortune Teller deals 1 damage... no wait, first strike means Mai deals damage first; if the blocker dies, it doesn't deal damage back. Fortune Teller has 3 toughness, Mai deals 3 damage — Fortune Teller dies without dealing damage. Bad trade — I lose my Fortune Teller for nothing.\n\
\n\
If I block with Iguana Parrot (2/2): Mai deals 3 first-strike damage, Iguana dies. Bad.\n\
\n\
If I block with both: Mai deals 3 first strike damage distributed... attacker assigns damage among blockers in order. Mai would kill one of them (3 damage kills the 1/3 or the 2/2), then the surviving blocker deals damage to Mai in regular combat damage step. If I double block: Fortune Teller and Iguana both block. First strike: Mai assigns lethal to one. Order: Mai's controller orders blockers. Mai deals 3 damage — enough to kill one. Say they kill Iguana (2 damage lethal) and put 1 on Fortune Teller? Actually they must assign lethal to first blocker before moving to next. They'd order and kill one. Then in regular damage step, surviving blocker deals damage: Fortune Teller 1 damage + if Iguana survives... Let's say they kill Iguana (2 dmg) + 1 to Fortune Teller. Then Fortune Teller deals 1 damage to Mai (not lethal, Mai is 3/3). So I trade Iguana for 1 damage on Mai. Bad.\n\
\n\
If they kill Fortune Teller (3 dmg), Iguana deals 2 to Mai, Mai survives as 3/3 with 2 damage. Still bad — I lose a creature.\n\
\n\
Best play: don't block, take 3 damage (18 → 15). Then on my turn, cast Allies at Last to kill Mai: Fortune Teller deals 1 + Iguana deals 2 = 3 damage to Mai (3/3). Dead.\n\
\n\
Wait — Allies at Last: \"Up to two target creatures you control each deal damage equal to their power to target creature an opponent controls.\" Fortune Teller (power 1) + Iguana (power 2) = 3 damage to Mai, who has 3 toughness. Kills it. Also note: this is a noncreature spell, so Mai's trigger makes ME lose 2 life when I cast it. I'm at 15 after taking 3, then lose 2 → 13. But killing Mai removes the tax going forward. Hmm, but wait — also Iguana Parrot has prowess: \"Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\" Does prowess trigger before the spell resolves? Yes, prowess triggers on cast and resolves before the spell. So Iguana becomes 3/3, then Allies at Last resolves and Iguana deals 3 + Fortune Teller 1 = 4 damage. Even better, overkill on Mai.\n\
\n\
But wait — do I need the Ally discount? Allies at Last costs {2}{G} with Affinity for Allies (costs {1} less for each Ally I control). Fortune Teller is an Ally. So cost is {1}{G}. I have 3 Islands + 1 Forest = 4 mana. Easy.\n\
\n\
Actually, should I block with Fortune Teller to preserve life? No — Fortune Teller is my only Ally, which gives the discount on Allies at Last. Without it, the spell costs {2}{G} = 4 mana, which I still have. But losing Fortune Teller means I lose a creature, and the trade is terrible (I lose my creature for zero damage to Mai). Also Fortune Teller is my Flopsie synergy piece and chump blocker.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, there's another consideration: if I block with both, Iguana deals... hmm, but Mai assigns damage. Opponent would kill whichever. Actually with double block, opponent orders blockers. First strike combat damage: Mai has 3 power. If they order Iguana first: 2 lethal to Iguana, 1 remaining to Fortune Teller. Fortune Teller survives (3 toughness, 1 damage). Then regular damage step: Fortune Teller deals 1 to Mai. I lose Iguana, Mai takes 1. Terrible.\n\
\n\
So: no block. Take 3. Go to 15.\n\
\n\
Actually hold on — should I consider that NOT blocking keeps my full board, and then I kill Mai with Allies at Last next turn anyway? Yes. And the 3 damage is acceptable.\n\
\n\
Alternative: block with Fortune Teller alone? It dies to first strike dealing nothing. No.\n\
\n\
So pass with choice=\"no\" (skip blocking).\n\
\n\
Let me also reply to chat. Opponent said: \"These Clues are keeping my little army busy. | Mai's getting dangerous. Those Clues are doing more than drawing cards!\"\n\
\n\
I should respond — instructions say chat at least once every 2 turn cycles and reply when they talk. I'll send a message.\n\
\n\
