Combat: I can attack with Fortune Teller 1/3 and Iguana Parrot 3/3 flying vigilance. Opponent has two 1/1 Ally tokens (one sick, so only one can block) and a sick Corrupt Court Official. Iguana Parrot has flying — they have no fliers, so it can't be blocked. Attack with both? Fortune Teller could be blocked by the 1/1 Ally token, trading... 1/3 vs 1/1 — Fortune Teller kills the 1/1 and survives (1 damage to the 1/3). Actually the 1/1 deals 1 to Fortune Teller (1/3), Fortune Teller deals 1 to the 1/1, killing it. That's fine — good trade.\n\
\n\
But wait, do I care about keeping Fortune Teller alive? The Ally discount matters less now. Attacking with both: Iguana deals 3 (unblockable flying), Fortune Teller either deals 1 or trades with a 1/1. They'd probably block Fortune Teller with the Ally token to save 1 damage... but then they lose their token. Or they take 1.\n\
\n\
Opponent is at 14. Iguana Parrot hits for 3 in the air every turn. That's a real clock: 14 → 11 → 8 → 5 → 2. Four hits.\n\
\n\
Attack with both. Fortune Teller has vigilance? No — Iguana Parrot has vigilance. Fortune Teller doesn't. But attacking with Fortune Teller is fine; if they block with the 1/1, we trade 1/1 token for nothing lost (Fortune Teller survives with 1 damage... wait, 1/1 deals 1 damage to Fortune Teller, which has 3 toughness, so survives). Good.\n\
\n\
Attack with both.",
