      "thinking": "I'm at 1 life, opponent at 18. I have a Clue crack on the stack. The log said I was cracking my Clue to dig. Now I need to respond/draw.\n\
\n\
Current board: I have Forest (untapped), Island p8 untapped, Meditation Pools untapped, Island p6 and p7 tapped. So I have 3 mana available: Forest (G), Island (U), Meditation Pools (G or U).\n\
\n\
My hand: Flopsie {4}{G}{G} (4/4), Forecasting Fortune Teller {1}{U} 1/3, Katara {2}{U} 2/3, Waterbender Ascension {1}{U}.\n\
\n\
Opponent: tapped out mostly, has Fire Nation Drill (9/6 with counters, tapped, crewed until end of turn... it will uncrew). Ally tokens: 2/2, 1/1, 1/1, 1/1 (one summoning sick). Obsessive Pursuit, Tolls of War. Untapped: Plains p67, Obsessive Pursuit, Tolls, one Plains.\n\
\n\
The Clue draw is on the stack. I should let it resolve. The pending action — stack has the Clue ability. I need to pass priority to let it resolve.\n\
\n\
The instruction says call pass_priority. Let me pass priority to resolve the Clue draw.\n\
\n\
Key strategic considerations: I'm at 1 life. Opponent has Obsessive Pursuit which triggers at upkeep — they lose 1 life, not me. Any attacker that gets through kills me. The Fire Nation Drill is 9/6 trample. I need blockers. My hand has Forecasting Fortune Teller (1/3) — a cheap blocker. Katara (2/3). Waterbender Ascension can make a creature unblockable.\n\
\n\
Win condition: I need to race. Opponent at 18. My creatures: Fortune Teller 1/3, Katara 2/3. Flopsie 4/4 needs 6 mana including GG — I have Forest + Meditation Pools for green, so next turn with 5 lands... currently I have 5 lands total (Forest, 3 Islands, Meditation Pools). Next turn I'd have 6 if I draw a land or play one from hand — no land in hand.\n\
\n\
Actually the key question: after drawing from the Clue, decide what to cast with my 3 mana (U, G, U/G). Options:\n\
- Forecasting Fortune Teller {1}{U}: 1/3 blocker + Clue token (more digging)\n\
- Katara {2}{U}: 2/3 blocker\n\
- Waterbender Ascension {1}{U}: setup for unblockable later\n\
\n\
I'm at 1 life facing a 9/6 trample + 4 tokens. I need chump blockers desperately. Fortune Teller gives a blocker plus a Clue. That's probably the play. Then possibly Waterbender Ascension too (2+... 1U + 1U = need two blue: Island p8 + Meditation Pools for U, Forest pays... Fortune Teller {1}{U} = Forest(G)? No, {1} can be any. So Island for U, Forest for 1. Then Waterbender Ascension {1}{U}: Meditation Pools for U and... only Forest left tapped... I have Forest, Island p8, Meditation Pools = 3 mana. Fortune Teller costs 2 (1+U), Ascension costs 2 (1+U). Total 4 mana. Can't do both with 3 mana.\n\
\n\
So choose one. Fortune Teller: blocker + clue. Katara: 2/3 blocker. Hmm. Fortune Teller seems best — chump + card.\n\
\n\
Wait — but also Mai is dead so no noncreature tax.\n\
\n\
Let me pass priority to resolve the Clue first and see what I draw.",
