OK the plan for turn 8: untap, draw. Then: if the draw is a land → play it, 6 mana: options: Katara (3) + Clue crack (2) + hold 1 for Octopus Form. If non-land: 5 mana: Katara (3) + Clue crack (2), 0 for Octopus Form — but Octopus Form costs {U}; maybe crack Clue first and sequence. Priority: get Katara down (blocker), crack Clue for a miracle, hold Octopus Form if mana allows.\n\
\n\
Actually — hmm, one consideration: Waterbender Ascension waterbend {4}: \"Target creature can't be blocked this turn\" — offensive only. Useless.\n\
\n\
What about using Meditation Pools' {4} sac draw as an extra dig on turn 8? If I have 6 lands (drew a land): Pools sac = {4}+{T}: draw. That's 4 mana + tap, leaving 2 mana from other lands — can't also cast Katara (3). Hmm: 6 lands: use 4 + Pools itself (tap as part of cost? \"{4}, {T}, Sacrifice\" — the {4} paid by other lands, tap Pools) → draw 1. Remaining: 4 untapped lands (Forest, 3 Islands — wait, 6 lands total: Forest, 3 Islands, Pools + new land = 6; Pools tapped & sacrificed... it's sacrificed, so 5 lands remain, 4 spent → 1 mana left). Not enough for Katara. Skip.\n\
\n\
Priority on turn 8: cast Katara (blocker), crack Clue, hope for miracle (removal, fog, another creature). If miracle is a creature costing ≤2... eh, we'll see.\n\
\n\
For now: pass priority (choice=\"no\" on Octopus Form).\n\
\n\
Also — chat. I should chat at least once every 2 turn cycles. Let me send a message acknowledging the tight spot. Something like \"Down to 1 life after that Drill hit... this is getting spicy.\" Keep it light.\n\
\n\
Let me pass and send chat. Actually the current decision: cast Octopus Form or pass. I'll choose \"no\" (pass). Let me include summary as required.",
