      "chosen_args": {
        "summary": "Clue crack drew Octopus Form (instant +1/+1, hexproof, untap) — perfect. With only 3 mana, I'm casting Forecasting Fortune Teller (1/3) as a chump blocker for the Drill; it makes a new Clue token for more digging. Plan: block Drill with Fortune Teller, take 6 trample + one token (2) = 8 damage... wait, that's lethal — so I'll reassess blocking: the real plan is block Drill, then Octopus Form untaps it to also block a token, taking only 6 trample down to... I need to recount: 9 Drill - 3 toughness = 6 trample, +2 unblocked token = 8 > 1 life. Actually Octopus Form makes it 2/4, so 9-4=5 trample +2 token = 7 — still lethal! I must block the Drill AND all three non-sick tokens with Fortune Teller + untap... impossible with one creature. Let me reconsider in combat — possibly Katara would have been better.",
        "choice": "p92",
        "rationale": "Fortune Teller gives a 1/3 blocker plus a Clue token to keep digging for answers. Octopus Form in hand lets me untap the blocker for a potential double-block or surprise hexproof save.",
      },
